  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "molecular-graph-18ef",
  "summary": "Recent preprints pair graph encoders with knowledge graphs, sequence embeddings, and retrosynthetic priors for property and interaction prediction.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is graph-structured learning in which domain knowledge is encoded as explicit graph topology or constraints rather than learned from raw features alone. GastroDL-Fusion pairs GIN-encoded protein-ligand graphs with ProtBERT/ESM sequence embeddings for binding prediction, while ECLIPSE applies heterogeneous graph transformers over the CROssBAR biomedical knowledge graph for compound-protein interactions. DeepDR integrates several deep models with a knowledge graph of 5.9M edges and 107 relation types for repositioning, and GCNMM uses meta-paths and mutual information objectives for latent drug-target interactions. PyrMol most explicitly couples chemistry priors, fusing functional group, pharmacophore and retrosynthetic knowledge into a hierarchical graph network for property prediction. GONNECT, a GO-constrained autoencoder on TCGA RNA-seq, is a useful counterpoint: its GO structure adds little beyond randomized or unconstrained baselines, so prior-knowledge constraints do not guarantee gains.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-13"
}
